  "slug": "missing-protein-protrec2-b54a",
  "summary": "Preprints now formalize attractor coherence and feedback design rules for biomolecular circuits, alongside in silico modeling of hepatic lineage induction.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is formal, mechanism-level modelling of gene regulatory dynamics, in which network structure is translated into quantitative and testable statements. The Boolean study formalizes attractor coherence and reports that canalization makes attractors less stable than their basins, analyzing 122 curated networks alongside random-network simulations. The positive-feedback paper offers a block-diagram framework that yields a design rule for feedback strength, with thresholds and hysteresis. The hepatic study applies a minimal network containing HNF4A, FOXA2 and CEBPA to simulate direct and reprogrammed lineage induction. The set is heterogeneous in scope, and the shared element is the use of explicit computational models of regulatory logic. What is new is the attempt to connect topology-level principles to design guidance and to lineage-level outcomes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-13"
}
